hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27574","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Judamah bint Wahb narrated to her that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I intended to forbid ghilah until I recalled that the Persians and Romans do it and it does not harm their children."
"27575","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, from Urwah, from Aishah, from Judamah bint Wahb al-Asadiyyah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I intended to forbid ghilah until I recalled that the Persians and Romans do that and it does not harm their children."
"27576","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Aishah, from Judamah bint Wahb al-Asadiyyah, and she was among the first emigrant women, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked about coitus interruptus. He said: It is the hidden infanticide."
"27577","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, and he mentioned it."
